div.p:
I do not think that the craft is, as yet, prepared
                    for such work, but it seems to me that she might be. She is about a 150 tons,
                    brigantine, or brig, schooner-rig—stern rather old style, having been ornamented
                    once with carving and gilding, which is now painted out; semi-clipper bow, with
                    a little gilding; very square yards; black funnel close before mainmast;
                    quarter-boats slung pretty high, and one of them varnished wood-color.
